  <h3>Making Healthy Choices at Qdoba</h3>
  <div class="seo-callout-box">
    <h4>Bowl instead of Burrito</h4>
    <p>Skips the tortilla entirely. Saves ~300 calories.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="seo-callout-box">
    <h4>Fajita Veggies or Beans instead of Rice</h4>
    <p>Adds fiber while trimming calories. Saves 170-190 calories.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="seo-callout-box">
    <h4>Pico de Gallo or Salsa instead of Cheese & Sour Cream</h4>
    <p>Flavor with almost no sodium. Saves 100-150 calories.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h3>
  <div class="seo-faq-accordion">
    <details>
      <summary>How many calories are in a Qdoba-style bowl?</summary>
      <p>A standard Grilled Chicken Bowl with rice, black beans, pico, and cheese runs around 650 calories with 47g of protein.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How many calories are in a Qdoba-style burrito?</summary>
      <p>A loaded Chicken Burrito with rice, beans, pico, and cheese runs about 950 calories.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What's the healthiest order?</summary>
      <p>A Grilled Chicken Salad with black beans, pico de gallo, and guacamole, no dressing, no cheese, comes in around 435 calories with 39g of protein and 19g of fiber.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can I build a keto or low-carb order?</summary>
      <p>Yes, a Steak Keto Bowl runs around 385 calories with roughly 14g of total carbs.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="brand-content wrap">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow"><span></span> Qdoba calories, simply</div>
    <h2>Plan the treat.<br><em>Keep the joy.</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div>
    <p>This Qdoba calorie calculator helps you compare popular bowl and burrito options before you order. Choose a base, select proteins and toppings, and use the instant result as a practical guide for your day.</p>
    <p>Food and drink nutrition can vary by location. For allergies or exact ingredient lists, always check Qdoba’s official information directly.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="faq wrap mini">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow"><span></span> FAQs</div>
    <h2>Qdoba<br><em>questions.</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="questions">
    <details open>
      <summary>Does portion size change calories?<b>+</b></summary>
      <p>Usually, yes. Double protein or extra rice can meaningfully change calories and macros. This calculator applies a typical adjustment for the selected portion options.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Are salsas and sides included?<b>+</b></summary>
      <p>The displayed base is an estimate for the listed item. You can add sides like chips and guac manually to your order.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is this an official Qdoba tool?<b>+</b></summary>
      <p>No. NutriRoute is independent and is not affiliated with Qdoba. This page is for information only.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
